### MetIQAPI SDK
The MetIQAPI SDK provides a convenient way to interact with the MetIQ API. This SDK allows you to manage use cases, perform bulk chat operations, upload files, and more.
## Installation
To use the MetIQAPI SDK, simply clone this repository and import the MetIQAPI class into your project.
git clone <repository-url>
##Usage
# Initialization
To initialize the MetIQAPI class, you need to provide the base_url and token.
```python
from metiq_api import MetIQAPI

base_url = "https://api.metiq.com"
token = "your_api_token"

api = MetIQAPI(base_url, token)
```

## Methods
# Create Use Case
Creates a new use case.
```python
usecase_config = {
    "name": "New Use Case",
    "description": "Description of the use case"
}
response = api.create_usecase(usecase_config)
print(response)
```

# Delete Use Case
Deletes an existing use case by its ID.
```python
usecase_id = "usecase_id"
status_code = api.delete_usecase(usecase_id)
print(status_code)
```

# Bulk Chat
Performs a bulk chat operation by uploading a file.
```python
usecase_id = "usecase_id"
file_path = "path/to/your/file.txt"
response = api.bulk_chat(usecase_id, file_path)
print(response)
```
# Get Bulk Chat
Retrieves the status of a bulk chat operation.
```python
usecase_id = "usecase_id"
response = api.get_bulk_chat(usecase_id)
print(response)
```
# File Upload
Uploads a file to a specific use case.
```python
usecase_id = "usecase_id"
file_path = "path/to/your/file.txt"
response = api.file_upload(usecase_id, file_path)
print(response)
```
# Get Status
Retrieves the status of a file upload.
```python
usecase_id = "usecase_id"
file_name = "file_name.txt"
response = api.get_status(usecase_id, file_name)
print(response)
```
# Cancel Bulk Chat
Cancels a bulk chat operation.
```python
usecase_id = "usecase_id"
file_name = "file_name.txt"
response = api.cancel_bulk_chat(usecase_id, file_name)
print(response)
```

# Chat
Performs a chat operation.

## Chat v1
```python
usecase_id = "usecase_id"
completion_v1 = {
    "message": "Hello, how can I help you?"
}
response = api.chat(usecase_id, completion_v1)
print(response)
```

## Chat v2
Performs a v2 chat operation.
```python
usecase_id = "usecase_id"

completion_v2 = {
        "prompt": {
                "role": "Agent",
                "parts": [
                        {"content": "string", "type": "Text"}
                ],
                "toolCallResponses": [
                        {"id": "string", "role": "Agent", "content": "string", "intent": "string"}
                ],
                "intent": "string",
        },
        "history": [
                {
                        "Role": "User",
                        "Parts": [{"Content": "Hello", "Type": "Text"}],
                        "Intent": None,
                },
                {
                        "Role": "Agent",
                        "Content": "Hi there!",
                        "Id": "123",
                        "Created": "2023-01-01T00:00:00Z",
                },
        ],
        "groundings": ["3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6"],
        "functions": [
                {"name": "string", "description": "string", "parametersSchema": "string"}
        ],
        "filters": {
                "additionalProp1": ["string"],
                "additionalProp2": ["string"],
                "additionalProp3": ["string"],
        },
        "context": {"Filename": ["string"]},
}

response = api.chat_v2(usecase_id, completion_v2)
print(response)
```

# Embeddings
Generates embeddings for a given request.
```python
usecase_id = "usecase_id"
embedding_request = {
    "text": "Sample text for embedding"
}
response = api.embeddings(usecase_id, embedding_request)
print(response)
```
# Search
Performs a search operation.
```python
usecase_id = "usecase_id"
query = {
    "query": "Search query"
}
response = api.search(usecase_id, query)
print(response)
```
# Get Use Case
Retrieves details of a specific use case.
```python
usecase_id = "usecase_id"
response = api.get_usecase(usecase_id)
print(response)
```
# List Use Cases
Lists all available use cases.
```python
response = api.list_usecases()
print(response)
```
# Get Use Case Settings
Retrieves the settings of a specific use case.
```python
usecase_id = "usecase_id"
response = api.get_usecase_settings(usecase_id)
print(response)
```
# Update Use Case Settings
Updates the settings of a specific use case.
```python
usecase_id = "usecase_id"
usecase_config = {
    "setting_key": "setting_value"
}
response = api.update_usecase_settings(usecase_id, usecase_config)
print(response)
```
## Logging
The SDK uses Python's built-in logging module to log detailed information about each request and response. Logs are written to both the console and a file named metiq_api.log.
